r('W4', 'BOARD: Pi 3 B at 10.237.27.215, 8 GB spare with the monitor candidate image', 'spi_poc_test --wake-core1 twice on the Monitor build', 'baseline/board_checks_monitor_candidate_20261107.txt: both calls refused 0xffff000a (NOT_SUPPORTED) and the Core 1 heartbeat kept rising (monitor event LEGACY_CMD_REFUSED detail 13); AND baseline/board_W4_alreadyon_nomonitor_20261109.txt: on the original non-monitor image (Sep-20, sha256 014bb983...) three consecutive wake calls each returned PSCI status -4 = ALREADY_ON (Core 1 is already diverted at boot); the monitor command 20 was refused there (BAD_PARAMETERS), confirming the build', 'PASS', "Both halves verified on the board: refusal on the Monitor build, ALREADY_ON on the non-monitor build (the wake tool prints FAIL for a non-zero status; -4 is the expected ALREADY_ON). The cmp read-back of this particular flash was not shown to me; the image was identified by behaviour.")
r('W7', 'BOARD: Pi 3 B at 10.237.27.215, 8 GB spare with the monitor TEST-STATISTICS image + W7 trigger (test command 25 op 4, magic value, client word I-ACCEPT-FORCED-PANIC); approved by the user on 2026-11-09', 'tstats_probe_w7 w7 I-ACCEPT-FORCED-PANIC: Core 1 panics itself at its next attempt, before taking the lock; then status polled for 5 s, 500 PTA calls, Linux checks', 'baseline/board_W7_before_20261109.txt (healthy baseline) and board_W7_after_20261109.txt: Core 1 stopped (poll_count frozen at 15566487553; core1_poll_age grew 1.5 s, 3.1 s, 4.6 s, 6.1 s, 7.6 s); the PTA kept answering SUCCESS on every call (500 calls after the panic: BUSY 0, errors 0, p50 3865 us, 0 lock timeouts, skip_total unchanged) so the lock was not left held; Linux stayed up (SSH, uptime, online CPUs 0,2-3, 93 processes, no kernel messages)', 'PASS', "Finding: with Core 1 dead nothing evaluates deadlines, so there is no MON_STARVED or heartbeat-timeout event and starved stays 0; the ONLY indicator is the growing core1_poll_age_ticks / 'core1 last poll N ms ago' in command 20 page 0, which the consumer must watch (design consequence recorded in the evidence file). Core 1 stays dead until the Pi is power-cycled. Test build only; no UART, so the panic message itself was not seen.")
r('X9', 'BOARD: Pi 3 B at 10.237.27.215, 8 GB spare with the monitor TEST-STATISTICS image (test-only firmware, hardened profile)', 'tstats_probe x9 200: Core 1 holds the lock 10 ms (test hold request), the status call is issued at once', 'baseline/teststats_X9_20261107.txt: status call BUSY 200 of 200 (fail-closed); wait ended at 1002.45 us after 384 attempts (383 attempts per ms; the 1 ms time bound ended the wait, not the 2000-attempt cap); Core 1 hold 10000.73 us', 'PASS', "Measured on the test-statistics build, not on the production hardened image (test code is excluded from it by a guard). Calibration: about 383 lock attempts per ms while waiting, so the 2000-attempt cap is a pure backstop. Frames/holds are simulated, not CAN-bus traffic.")
r('Y10', 'BOARD: Pi 3 B at 10.237.27.215, 8 GB spare with the monitor candidate image', 'two reads of command 20 page 0, 5 s apart, passes and skip_total over now_ticks', 'baseline/board_checks_monitor_candidate_20261107.txt: 13.29 million passes/s = 75.2 ns per pass, about 51,900 lock attempts/s, 1 collision in 5 s (two runs agree)', 'PARTIAL', 'Pass duration and collision count measured. Hold time was NOT measured (needs test-only code). Finding: the design assumed 2.435 us per pass and a lock attempt every 0.62 ms; the monitor loop runs 32 times faster, so Core 1 now attempts the lock about every 19 us. See COMPONENT_2_2_FINAL_CLOSURE.md section 14.')
r('H3', 'BOARD: Pi 3 B at 10.237.27.215, 8 GB spare with the monitor TEST-STATISTICS image (test-only firmware, hardened profile)', 'tstats_probe reset, latency_probe 100000 calls, tstats_probe dump (CNTPCT stamps at lock and unlock); repeated under 3 busy loops and during a 180 s frame soak', 'baseline/teststats_H3_cadence256_20261107.txt, teststats_H3_cpuload_20261107.txt, teststats_H3_soak_20261107.txt, teststats_cadence_sweep_20261107.txt: longest PTA hold 6.30 us (idle), 6.51 us (CPU load), 5.68 us (soak), 7.24 us (largest over the cadence sweep); Core 1 hold max 0.21-0.31 us; all PTA holds fall in the 3.3-6.6 us bucket; 0 BUSY, 0 lock timeouts', 'PASS', "Target was under 100 us: met with a factor of about 14 margin. The histogram is coarse (factor 2), so 'p99' is an upper bucket edge, but the maximum is exact. Measured on the test-statistics build, so the stamps add a few ticks; the production image has no stamps. The earlier inference of about 11.6 us per call was too high and is withdrawn.")
# ---------------- deferred (1)
r('Z8', G+': rpi3_mon_pta_invoke legacy policy', H+':417 "LG1/LG4 refused ids 0,3,6,7,13,14"; :422 "LG2 chip A debug readers: refused when hardened; allowed with an event in the debug profile"; :426 "LG3"', R+'; mutants "WRITE_REG32 no longer refused", "hardened profile allows the debug readers", "commands 12 refused", "legacy refusal logs nothing" caught', 'PASS', HOSTLIM+" The original row names 4, 6, 7, 14, 15, 16; the implemented policy (decisions DEC-IF-8 to 10) refuses 6, 7, 14 always and 4, 15, 16 in the hardened profile, logging them in the debug profile. Debug profile built (final_on_debug) but behaviour tested only through the mock flag.")
assert list(orig) and set(rows) == set(orig), (set(orig) ^ set(rows))
cnt = collections.Counter(v[3] for v in rows.values())
out = []
out.append("# COMPONENT_2_2_INVENTORY.md - evidence mapping of the original 53 checks\n")
out.append("Date: 2026-11-07 (regenerated after the H1 fix). Generated by `source_tests/make_inventory.py`: the 53 IDs, requirement texts and kinds are parsed from the original table in `MONITOR_STATE_DESIGN.md` section 4j (nothing renamed, nothing deleted). The evidence column is hand-written and every cited file exists in `Part_E_Verification/`.\n")
out.append("Result vocabulary: **PASS** = the requirement as written was verified by the cited real evidence; **PARTIAL** = part of the row is verified on hardware and the named rest is NOT RUN; **FAIL** = a real defect was found; **NOT RUN** = needs the board or was not executed; **NOT VERIFIED** = evidence insufficient (none in this list). Evidence classes: HOST = real monitor source compiled for the host with a mock platform (not hardware); STATIC = pattern check on comment-stripped source; OBJECT = inspection of the compiled Monitor-ON `tee.elf`; BUILD = OP-TEE scratch build.\n")
out.append("**Evidence vintage.** Rows cite the `*_closure_20261107.txt` logs, produced before the H1 fix. The fix changed only `rpi3_mon_frame_store` (3 lines added, 1 removed). All suites were rerun on the fixed source with identical results: `run_h1fix_20261107.txt` (406 checks, 0 failed), `static_h1fix_20261107.txt` (55 pass including the 2 new object-code checks), `mutation_h1fix_20261107.txt` (137 of 140, the same 3 equivalent survivors), rebuilt OFF/ON/debug images (`build_scratch/final_*_h1.log`, 0 warnings).\n")
out.append("## Summary\n")
out.append("| Result | Rows |\n|---|---|")
for k in ('PASS', 'PARTIAL', 'FAIL', 'NOT RUN', 'NOT VERIFIED'): out.append("| %s | %d |" % (k, cnt.get(k, 0)))
